        "original_id": "190ce861-ab35-5df8-ac25-eae805d9db19",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Steven Weinberg, Abdus Salam, Sheldon Glashow, Jogesh Pati\n- Roles: theoretical physicist, Nobel laureate, professor, board member\n- Organizations: Boston University, Harvard University, Bulletin of the Atomic Scientists\n- Concepts: electroweak unification, asymptotic safety, quantum gravity, UV completion, preons\n\nFacts:\n- Steven Weinberg was born on May 3, 1933.\n- In 1974, Jogesh Pati and Abdus Salam coined the word \"preon.\"\n- Steven Weinberg is an American theoretical physicist and a Nobel laureate in Physics.\n- Steven Weinberg received the Nobel Prize in Physics with Abdus Salam and Sheldon Glashow for contributions to the unification of the weak force and electromagnetic interaction between elementary particles.\n- Sheldon Glashow is the Metcalf Professor of Mathematics and Physics at Boston University.\n- Sheldon Glashow is Higgins Professor of Physics, Emeritus, at Harvard University.\n- Sheldon Glashow is a member of the Board of Sponsors for the Bulletin of the Atomic Scientists.\n- Steven Weinberg originally proposed asymptotic safety to find a theory of quantum gravity.\n- The concept of a nontrivial fixed point as a possible UV completion can also be applied to other field theories, especially perturbatively nonrenormalizable theories.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "dd98e09d-1241-5367-a534-8a974efac267",
        "text": "Page: Steven Weinberg. Sentence: Steven Weinberg (born May 3, 1933) is an American theoretical physicist and Nobel laureate in Physics for his contributions with Abdus Salam and Sheldon Glashow to the unification of the weak force and electromagnetic interaction between elementary particles.\nPage: Sheldon Lee Glashow. Sentence: He is the Metcalf Professor of Mathematics and Physics at Boston University and Higgins Professor of Physics, Emeritus, at Harvard University, and is a member of the Board of Sponsors for the \"Bulletin of the Atomic Scientists\".\nPage: Asymptotic safety in quantum gravity. Sentence: Although originally proposed by Steven Weinberg to find a theory of quantum gravity, the idea of a nontrivial fixed point providing a possible UV completion can be applied also to other field theories, in particular to perturbatively nonrenormalizable ones.\nPage: Preon. Sentence: The word was coined by Jogesh Pati and Abdus Salam in 1974.",
